GOOGLE ADS API DESIGN DOCUMENT
Maze Mídia — Internal Marketing Dashboard
Version 1.0 — May 2026

================================================================
1. COMPANY OVERVIEW
================================================================

Company Name: Maze Mídia
Website: https://mazemidia.com.br
Contact Email: geovane@mazemidia.com.br

Maze Mídia is a Brazilian digital marketing agency that manages
Google Ads campaigns on behalf of its clients. The agency
operates as a certified Google Ads partner and manages multiple
client accounts through a single MCC (Manager) account.

================================================================
2. TOOL OVERVIEW
================================================================

Tool Name: Maze Mídia Internal Marketing Dashboard
Type: Internal reporting dashboard (not distributed externally)
Users: Internal agency employees only

The tool is a private web dashboard built to consolidate
marketing performance data from multiple platforms (Google Ads,
Meta Ads, Google Analytics 4, and CRM) into a single reporting
interface for internal use by the Maze Mídia team.

================================================================
3. PURPOSE AND USE CASE
================================================================

The dashboard is used exclusively for:

- Monitoring campaign performance metrics (spend, impressions,
  clicks, conversions) across client accounts
- Generating internal performance reports
- Tracking ROI and key marketing KPIs for client accounts
- Identifying trends and anomalies in campaign data

The tool does NOT:
- Create or modify campaigns
- Manage bids or budgets
- Access or store any end-user personal data
- Distribute data to third parties

================================================================
4. DATA FLOW
================================================================

Step 1: Data Collection
A Python script runs daily via GitHub Actions (automated CI/CD)
and calls the Google Ads API to retrieve campaign-level
performance metrics for the past 90 days.

API Resource queried: campaign
Metrics collected per campaign per day:
  - campaign.name
  - metrics.cost_micros (spend)
  - metrics.clicks
  - metrics.impressions
  - metrics.conversions
  - segments.date

Step 2: Data Storage
The collected data is aggregated and stored as a JSON file
(summary.json) in a private GitHub repository. No raw API
responses are stored.

Step 3: Data Visualization
The JSON file is read by a static HTML dashboard hosted on
GitHub Pages (private access). The dashboard displays charts
and KPI cards for internal review.

================================================================
5. API USAGE
================================================================

Endpoints used:
- GoogleAdsService.Search (read-only)

Query example:
  SELECT campaign.name, metrics.cost_micros, metrics.clicks,
         metrics.impressions, metrics.conversions, segments.date
  FROM campaign
  WHERE segments.date BETWEEN '2026-01-01' AND '2026-05-11'
    AND campaign.status != 'REMOVED'
    AND metrics.cost_micros > 0

Access type: Read-only (no write operations)
Authentication: OAuth 2.0 with offline refresh token
Token storage: Stored securely as environment variables in
               GitHub Actions Secrets (never exposed in code)

================================================================
6. CAMPAIGN TYPES SUPPORTED
================================================================

The tool collects and reports on all active campaign types:
- Search
- Performance Max
- Display
- Video
- Demand Gen

================================================================
7. SECURITY AND DATA HANDLING
================================================================

- OAuth credentials stored as encrypted GitHub Secrets
- No end-user personal data is collected or stored
- API calls are read-only (no account modifications possible)
- Dashboard access is restricted to internal team members
- No third-party data sharing

================================================================
8. INFRASTRUCTURE
================================================================

- Language: Python 3.11
- Automation: GitHub Actions (daily scheduled job)
- Dashboard: Static HTML + JavaScript (Chart.js)
- Hosting: GitHub Pages (private repository)
- Authentication: Google OAuth 2.0

